\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {B-FAIS}\xspace  converts a corrupted multivariate context into a validity-gated block-wise completion before frozen-TSFM forecasting. At historical origins (top), complete-candidate forecast losses and second-order counterfactual effects train the unary rankers and pair model; at deployment (middle), six numbered steps extract blocks, shortlist candidates, collect pseudo-missing evidence, refine unary risks, coordinate the assignment, and assemble the completed context. The bottom ladder identifies the three one-factor changes used by the registered mechanism tests.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{\bfais converts a corrupted multivariate context into a validity-gated block-wise completion before frozen-TSFM forecasting. At historical origins (top), complete-candidate forecast losses and second-order counterfactual effects train the unary rankers and pair model; at deployment (middle), six numbered steps extract blocks, shortlist candidates, collect pseudo-missing evidence, refine unary risks, coordinate the assignment, and assemble the completed context. The bottom ladder identifies the three one-factor changes used by the registered mechanism tests}{figure.1}{}}
